        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kenneth Williams, Cheryl Campbell, Michael Sheen, Lou, Bob Hoskins\n- Works: Kenneth Williams: Fantabulosa!, Pennies From Heaven, Testament of Youth, Malice Aforethought, A Doll's House\n- Organizations: BBC Four, BBC, BAFTA, Olivier Awards\n- Roles: English comic actor, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Cheryl Campbell was born on 22 May 1949 and is an English actor of stage, film, and television.\n- In 1978, Cheryl Campbell starred opposite Bob Hoskins in the BBC drama Pennies From Heaven.\n- In 1980, Cheryl Campbell won the BAFTA TV Award for Best Actress for Testament of Youth and Malice Aforethought.\n- In 1982, Cheryl Campbell won the Olivier Award for Best Actress in a Revival for A Doll's House.\n- Kenneth Williams: Fantabulosa! is a 2006 BBC Four television play starring Michael Sheen as the English comic actor Kenneth Williams.\n- Kenneth Williams: Fantabulosa! is based on Kenneth Williams's own diaries.\n- In Kenneth Williams: Fantabulosa!, Cheryl Campbell plays Kenneth Williams's beloved mother, Lou.",
